17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Two-Variable Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1033 356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "59bac138-6475-51d1-971d-3bd216b92f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Rational Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1033 68 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050843 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6ae775b6-8adc-58c2-abd8-8374a1314249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $5ky-13=7$ for the variable $y$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ddcd149b-a90b-5ed2-923d-75e8a84ff145" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179465 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $y$. To do this, we first add $13$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5ky - 13 &= 7 \\\\\n5ky - 13 + 13 &= 7 + 13 \\\\\n5ky &= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $5k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5ky &= 20 \\\\\n\\frac{5ky}{5k} &= \\frac{20}{5k} \\\\\n\\frac{5ky}{5k} &= \\frac{20}{5k} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{20}{5k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{5 \\cdot 4}{5k} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5 \\cdot 4}{5k} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13902" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2$ for the variable $x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6eb1b4ba-3182-5ecc-8ae0-72ec27036b29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179466 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{4}kx + 9 &= 2 \\\\\n4 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}kx + 9) &= 4 \\cdot 2 \\\\\n3kx + 36 &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $x$. To do this, we first subtract $36$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3kx + 36 &= 8 \\\\\n3kx + 36 - 36 &= 8 - 36 \\\\\n3kx &= -28\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3kx &= -28 \\\\\n\\frac{3kx}{3k} &= \\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\\n\\frac{3kx}{3k} &= \\frac{-28}{3k} \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{28}{3k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{ax}{5}$ for the variable $x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b35596e5-5914-502f-87dd-89348ab1664c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179468 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $x$. To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{3} &= -\\frac{ax}{5} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} &= \\frac{-ax}{5} \\\\\n5 \\cdot 1 &= 3 \\cdot (-ax) \\\\\n5 &= -3ax\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5 &= -3ax \\\\\n\\frac{5}{-3a} &= \\frac{-3ax}{-3a} \\\\\n\\frac{5}{-3a} &= \\frac{-3ax}{-3a} \\\\\n- \\frac{5}{3a} &= x \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{5}{3a}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Equations With Unknown Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179626 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7c6535bf-7dd1-5231-a992-9aefb8066499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Equations Containing Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179627 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aefe9086-38a5-5055-9f95-56eafacf518b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Equations Using Cross Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179628 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "41be5b01-b9ea-576b-a7e5-d522b8b1dc88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Linear Equations With Unknown Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179890 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e4b9901d-88e7-5d69-a378-0f71f70c0310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180313 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180313 #edb/ref 1061 103208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180313 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fb33245e-3b63-52de-95bb-e6deb0330b74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180313 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180314 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180314 #edb/ref 1061 103209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180314 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d0ff4ba1-749b-5438-9506-e7f014aaceae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180314 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180315 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180315 #edb/ref 1061 103213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180315 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5e760b3f-b53b-5d1b-b4a7-1237dd923fd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180315 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180316 #edb/ref 1061 103219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180316 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7771c38-e5f5-5a62-86cb-500b9d46ebf3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180316 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180780 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following equation:\n\n$$\n2{\\color{red}m}{\\color{blue}t} = 1\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation has two variables, ${\\color{red}m}$ and ${\\color{blue}t}$. Suppose we want to solve the equation for the variable ${\\color{blue}t}$.\n\nTo isolate ${\\color{blue}t}$, we apply the multiplication principle and divide both sides of the equation by $2{\\color{red}m}$, treating ${\\color{red}m}$ as though it were a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2mt &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{2mt}{2m} &= \\frac{1}{2m} \\\\\n\\frac{2mt}{2m} &= \\frac{1}{2m} \\\\\nt &= \\frac{1}{2m}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we'll take a look at an example where we need to apply both the addition and multiplication principles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180780 #edb/ref 1065 8664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180780 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "841f1014-d389-5378-ab68-d2e1d2a95016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180780 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
